Push notifications for the native app (Android now, iOS later).

Base: zan-workspace main at e845ae6 "feat(notifications): add FCM web push notifications".
Apply from the web repo root:
    git apply --check native-push.patch
    git apply native-push.patch

What it changes:
- POST /api/notifications/devices accepts `platform` (PUSH_PLATFORM: 10 web, 20 Android, 30 iOS)
  and `appVersion`. Only browsers get the push_device cookie.
- DELETE /api/notifications/devices also reads { fid } from the JSON body, for the phone's logout.
- sendPush adds an `android` block (priority high, 24 h TTL) and an `apns` block (alert, thread-id,
  category, interruption level). Data gains `channel`, `type`, `entityType` and `entityId`.
- New src/constants/pushChannels.ts: the channel list and the event -> channel map. Copy it to the
  phone unchanged, like the other constants. src/constants/pushDevice.ts gains PUSH_PLATFORM.
- Label "Web Push" becomes "Push" (logs only).

Browsers keep working as before: they send no platform, keep the cookie, and read only title, body
and url. No new environment variables. No migration: old PushDevice rows count as browsers.

